			<div class="content" id="post-content-3167511">
									

<p>The level 4 chat logs are where it's revealed that once the computer they're operating on breaks down, they will quite possibly left in eternal isolation. Even from each other. That's dark as fuck. It's way darker than anything previously revealed in the SCP. I mean, crap, even <a href="/scp-3001">SCP-3001</a> at least had that red light! They won't even get that.</p>
<p>On top of that, grrgirl explicitly states that this isn't going to redeem them. The people they killed are going to stay dead. This isn't about redemption; this is about a group of teenagers staring at all this horror, all this darkness&#8230; and rather than just giving up, finding a way to make <em>peace</em> with it.</p>
<p>I'm tired of writing SCPs where everything is awful for everyone forever. It's not good for my brain.</p>
<p><strong>ETA:</strong> I mean, it's perfectly fine if this isn't your thing &#8212; but nobody's getting 'redeemed' here. All that's happening is a bunch of terrified kids are figuring out a way to be a little less scared.</p>

