<p>Thanks! I thought for a while about whether or not they're Thaumiel, and I finally settled on no for two reasons:</p>
<ul>
<li>It makes the ending harder to see coming (otherwise, I'd have to use some sort of format screw to hide the fact that they're Thaumiel).</li>
<li>I don't think the Foundation really trusts them. As WTF_STFU puts it: They're unstoppable nigh-immortal digitalized death-gods. O5 Council said yes only because if they turned them down, they might have flipped their shit &#8212; and the only way to stop them would have been to blow the computer up and hope it actually <em>does</em> neutralize them.</li>
</ul>
<p>TL;DR: The Foundation is letting them play MTF because they're good at it, and it gives them something to do (which makes them more predictable, and thusly easier to contain). But they're not Thaumiel because the Foundation perceives them as <em>way</em> too dangerous.</p>
<p>I imagine the Foundation has a remote-controlled kill-switch attached to SCP-2639-C &#8212; just in case.</p>

